# HOME COMING â€” response headers
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this automatically the moment you drop the
# folder in. On any other host it is simply ignored, which is harmless.

# The same policy applies to every page: the whole site, then these.
# - no page may be framed by another site, which stops clickjacking
# - no guessing of content types, which is a form-sniffing defence
# - the browser does not leak your page address when you follow a link out
# - after one visit, the browser refuses to ever try an unencrypted version
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the strict one, and it is only safe because
# the front end loads nothing it did not write itself. If you ever add a photo
# hosted somewhere else, add that domain to img-src below.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://cumgwfrjilghykgszblt.supabase.co https://api.web3forms.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

